Priority 6/10 : Adding a variadic system that is type-safe
    |> planned syntax would be the following:
        specify<typename T> // generics are never variadic
        void print(const char *const format, T... args) // T... doesn't mean "everything has type T", it means "everything has a distinct type T"
        {
            foreach (arg, args) // this syntax may change as it is still being thought about
            {
                // logic
            }
        }
    |> expanded at compile-time and the resulting C code will be specialized (monomorphization for variadics)
        ^^ (this can lead to code bloat) (note from future me [2026-08-19]; that doesn't fucking matter anymore with the current transpilation model)


